A||N||29||AusFiero||Stage 2. Would anybody buy this body kit if the price was right.||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||05-07-2001||10:39 AM||||I have managed to get further along with the design of the total body kit for the coupe and judging by the interest I best make it or never dare set foot in America through fear of lynching.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The new additions are a front spoiler, new mirrors, a larger rear spoiler and a lower rear bumper cover.<P>This would bring the kit up to a 15 piece kit for the serious Fiero modifier. Stage 3 will be coming soon.<P>The original post of Stage 1 of the kit is at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007256.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007256.html</A> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2unpainted.jpg"> <P>Below is Stage 2 painted in a new colour with the 5 spoke wheels also detail painted.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2painted.jpg"> <P>And please give me time on pricing... I don't want to rip you or me off.<BR> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-07-2001||10:41 AM||||Oh, my! Schweet!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierojunky||05-07-2001||10:59 AM||||Looks Great!! - If i could just make one suggestion - how difficult would it be to do something with the black sail pannels - they look out of perportion now.  And could we pick and chose what pieces we want or do we have to get them all.   ||||reg||14
Z||000003||ccollins||05-07-2001||10:59 AM||||I would be interested in the rear side scoops, rocker panels, and possibly rear wing if it would fit an '87 GT.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||05-07-2001||12:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierojunky:<BR><B>Looks Great!! - If i could just make one suggestion - how difficult would it be to do something with the black sail pannels - they look out of perportion now.  And could we pick and chose what pieces we want or do we have to get them all.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Firstly, sure pieces will be available separately. <P>I agree about the sail panels. Yours hasn't been the first suggestion to find a way to change it. So I canme up with some panels that would replace the existing sail panel "windows" and extend back into a section cut out of the forward edge of the notchback panel. These panels could also incorporate a hidden air intake in the lower right corner on the pic. Using this design they would not have to be moulded into or replace the notchback panel saving costly bodywork. The upper and right edges of the new panel would blend the rain gutter out rather than it just stopping abruptly.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2-1painted.jpg"> <BR>And yet another colour.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jake2m4||05-07-2001||12:35 PM||||That is awesome.  I would be interested in the door panels and scoops.  Depending on price and if I can scrape the money up when ever you get to production.  Keep us updated.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||1
